From 1ad67d40fbbce03ca933b89224b447fecb5afa1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:41:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] volumepathhandler: tear down block volumes on FreeBSD

FreeBSD has no block or loop devices, so mapping a block-mode volume
fails, as it should. Unmapping it then failed too: UnmapBlockVolume
starts with DetachFileDevice, which returned "not supported", and the
kubelet retried forever. A pod given a block-mode local PV never finished
terminating.

Give FreeBSD its own handler. Nothing can have been attached, so
DetachFileDevice has nothing to detach and succeeds, as Linux does when no
loop device holds the file; GetLoopDevice reports ErrDeviceNotFound.
AttachFileDevice still fails.
---
 .../volume_path_handler_freebsd.go            | 59 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../volume_path_handler_unsupported.go        |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/volume/util/volumepathhandler/volume_path_handler_freebsd.go

diff --git a/pkg/volume/util/volumepathhandler/volume_path_handler_freebsd.go b/pkg/volume/util/volumepathhandler/volume_path_handler_freebsd.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..81e4b367d0f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/volume/util/volumepathhandler/volume_path_handler_freebsd.go
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+//go:build freebsd
+
